    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 959,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Princess Beatrice of the United Kingdom\nPrincess Beatrice of the United Kingdom , ( Beatrice Mary Victoria Feodore ; later Princess Henry of Battenberg ; 14 April 1857 -- 26 October 1944 ) was the fifth daughter and youngest child of Queen Victoria and Prince Albert . King Felipe VI of Spain is her great-great-grandson . Beatrice was the last of Queen Victoria 's children to die , 65 years after the first , her sister Alice . Beatrice 's childhood coincided with Queen Victoria 's grief following the death of her husband Albert , Prince Consort on 14 December 1861 . As her elder sisters married and left their mother , Queen Victoria came to rely on the company of her youngest daughter , whom she called `` Baby '' for most of her childhood . Beatrice was brought up to stay with her mother always and she soon resigned herself to her fate . Queen Victoria was so set against her youngest daughter marrying that she refused to discuss the possibility ."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
